From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: system messages for every Windows Sockets error and the common COM results

FormatMessageW(FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_SYSTEM) failed with ERROR_MR_MID_NOT_FOUND for
all but 13 Windows Sockets errors and all but three HRESULTs: Lapce showed
'tcp connect error: OS Error 10051 (FormatMessageW() returned error 317)' (Rust's
std formats every OS error that way), Chromium-based programs logged 'Error (0x13D)
while retrieving error. (0x80004002)'. The message table now has text, in our own
words, for every Windows Sockets code winerror.h defines (WSAEINTR ..
WSA_QOS_RESERVED_PETYPE) and the common COM results (E_NOINTERFACE, E_POINTER,
E_ABORT, E_UNEXPECTED, E_PENDING .. RO_E_CLOSED, CLASS_E_*, REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG,
CO_E_NOT/ALREADYINITIALIZED, RPC_E_*, DISP_E_*), as Windows' table has.
HRESULT_FROM_WIN32 of a sockets error already folds to it.

Gate: test/syserrtext-gate.sh.
